      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It sounds like the desperate need for silence has consumed your entire identity, making the idea of a new beginning feel impossible by design. Sometimes the only way to reclaim yourself is not to rebuild from the inside out immediately, but to step outside the silence enough for the quiet noise of your own personhood to return. You don't have to save everyone you've ever been for yourself to start again; you only have to write a single new line for the first time you want to.",
